<h1>Unyap</h1>

<p><em>Impatience, now a browser extension.</em></p>

<p>You clicked for the answer, not for ten minutes of intro. Unyap is a Chrome extension for YouTube: it finds the part of a video that answers its title, and <strong>Unyap it</strong> jumps there. A strip over the progress bar marks filler, context and substance, and <strong>Next good part</strong> skips to the next useful bit. If the title is never answered, it tells you.</p>

<p>It runs in your browser with your own OpenAI API key. It uses OpenAI’s Decisions API, which answers every question about a video in a single request, so a new video costs about $0.001 and one you already analyzed costs nothing. Nothing is sent to me, and I store no data. Other AI providers are coming soon.</p>

<p>Coming soon to the Chrome Web Store. I built it at the DevDay Community Hackathon in Berlin, October 2026.</p>

